  "id": "ve71ss9",
  "title": "Chapter 16: Fundamental Rights",
  "order": 17,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fynsap6",
      "content": "Fundamental Rights are basic human freedoms guaranteed by the Constitution of India to all citizens. They are contained in Part III of the Constitution (Articles 12–35). These rights protect individual liberty and ensure equality before the law. Dr. B.R. Ambedkar called the Right to Constitutional Remedies the 'heart and soul of the Constitution'."
    },
