          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Article 18</p>",
            "<p>Abolition of titles</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "j95b864",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Exceptions to Right to Equality"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5yfisfh",
      "content": "• President and Governors enjoy immunity from court proceedings during their tenure."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tu5elwk",
      "content": "• Parliament can make special provisions for women and children."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bxts82e",
      "content": "• State can provide reservations for SC, ST and OBC."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ou2b477",
      "content": "• Diplomatic officials enjoy immunity."
    },
    {
      "id": "jfgwx5s",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Right to Freedom (Articles 19–22)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "no5fxf4",
      "content": "Article 19 provides six freedoms to citizens:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uk3vuse",
      "content": "• Freedom of speech and expression"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "k8u25oq",
      "content": "• Freedom to assemble peacefully"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9zb9twv",
      "content": "• Freedom to form associations or unions"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Article 32 is the very heart and soul of the Constitution.",
      "id": "37sibzb"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "30zqw1z",
      "content": "• Freedom to move freely throughout India"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c0st1h5",
      "content": "• Freedom to reside and settle in any part of India"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "olzr2h4",
      "content": "• Freedom to practice any profession or occupation"
    },
    {
      "id": "ijhvldj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Reasonable Restrictions"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "tm3xyls",
      "content": "• Security of the state"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "wmsjz1e",
      "content": "• Public order"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "s9mhhbh",
      "content": "• Morality"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cdaozv7",
      "content": "• Friendly relations with foreign states"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "i82qmnz",
      "content": "• Contempt of court"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Feature",
        "Supreme Court (Article 32)",
        "High Court (Article 226)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Scope of Jurisdiction",
          "Narrower: Can issue writs strictly for the enforcement of Fundamental Rights",
          "Wider: Can issue writs for Fundamental Rights as well as ordinary legal rights"
        ],
        [
          "Territorial Jurisdiction",
          "Wider: Applicable throughout the entire territory of India",
          "Narrower: Enforceable only within its specific state or territorial limit"
        ],
        [
          "Remedial Status",
          "Mandatory: Article 32 itself is a Fundamental Right, so the SC cannot refuse relief",
          "Discretionary: High Court may refuse to grant relief if alternative remedies exist"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "szyg3gw"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "jzuui5i",
      "content": "• Defamation"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fjjndoe",
      "content": "Article 20 protects against arbitrary punishment."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7u19fcw",
      "content": "Article 21 guarantees protection of life and personal liberty."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "34tsdv7",
      "content": "Article 21A provides the Right to Education (added by 86th Amendment)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ydh67zw",
      "content": "Article 22 protects against arbitrary arrest and detention."
    },
    {
