    {
      "id": "9a4vann",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Right to Constitutional Remedies (Articles 32–35)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "39njibj",
      "content": "Citizens can approach Supreme Court or High Court to enforce Fundamental Rights."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The Right to Property (Article 31) was deleted from the list of Fundamental Rights by the 44th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1978, making it a legal right under Article 300A.",
        "Fundamental Rights guaranteed under Articles 20 and 21 cannot be suspended even during a National Emergency.",
        "Article 32 provides for 5 types of writs: Habeas Corpus, Mandamus, Prohibition, Certiorari, and Quo-Warranto."
      ],
      "id": "8g8cvt7"
    },
    {
      "id": "i04cccf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Types of Writs"
    },
    {
      "id": "m39s2uj",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Writ</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Purpose</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Habeas Corpus</p>",
            "<p>Produce a person illegally detained</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mandamus</p>",
            "<p>Order to public authority to perform duty</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Prohibition</p>",
            "<p>Prevent lower court from exceeding jurisdiction</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Certiorari</p>",
            "<p>Transfer case from lower court to higher court</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Quo Warranto</p>",
            "<p>Challenge legality of holding public office</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "u2ls8c0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "EXAM Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o4lz1sw",
      "content": "• Fundamental Rights are given in Part III (Articles 12–35)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "benki3e",
      "content": "• Article 32 is called the heart and soul of the Constitution."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mbdaolb",
      "content": "• Article 17 abolishes untouchability."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "n0w1doa",
      "content": "• Right to Education added by 86th Amendment."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w3ngf2b",
      "content": "• There are currently six Fundamental Rights."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
